shape theory.mixing.source-destination : theory.mixing {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 9.2 (Structural Specification of a Transition).
// The structural content of a transformation M -> M' is determined
// by two independent quantities:
//
//   Source structure (c): degrees of freedom needed to specify the
//     shape's character before the transition.
//   Destination structure (d): the structural space across which
//     the transformation could distribute the shape.
//
// Definition 9.3 (Persistence Magnitude): p = c + d.
// Total structural dimension count of the transition.
//
// Source and destination are independent: specifying a source does
// not consume the destination space. The source projects onto the
// destination; it does not reduce it.
//
// Derives from: theory.mixing
  """
}
